kentik-network-monitoring is the Kentik network observability configuration and operations skill:
large-scale flow analytics, flow enrichment, the flow data model, DDoS detection and automated mitigation,
BGP route monitoring and hijack/leak/RPKI detection, Kentik NMS and Kentik Map, AI Insights, built-in
synthetic monitoring, and the REST/topXdata/Terraform/Python-SDK automation surface. It is a vendor ops
skill in the NMS family; the DESIGN/paradigm/platform-selection decision lives in
network-monitoring-selection (PR 1), to which this skill routes the design question back.
Skill licensed MIT (the primary-source licence).

Part of NMS family PR 2 of 3 (PRTG + Kentik, MIT single-source). Scope = full ops per the DNS +
Load-balancer precedent.

